{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ChiralityDualSpaceDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ChiralityDualSpaceDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_dual_space_derivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_dual_space_derivation","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L233-L246","doc":"**Term 5 of the unified mass formula.**\n\nIdentification of the per-crossing symmetric-channel dual-\nspace pairing with the paper's chirality factor `a_K`.\n\nDual-space identity per pn crossing:\n  τ_sym(σ) - τ_sym(σ⁻¹) = h.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] `prop:chirality-dual-space-derivation` §Derivation.\nRef: [kassel1995] Quantum Groups, Ch. III §2. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:chirality-dual-space-derivation","label":"prop:chirality-dual-space-derivation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_at_h_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_at_h_zero","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L219-L231","doc":"**Chirality factor at h = 0 equals 1.**\n\nAt the classical limit `q → 1` (`h = 0`), chirality disappears:\nevery per-crossing factor becomes `1`, so the total product is `1`.\nThis is consistent with the classical Jones-polynomial specialisation\nto the unknot bracket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_real","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L211-L217","doc":"**Chirality factor is real.**\n\nThe factor is a polynomial in `h` with integer coefficients,\nhence real for any real `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.he4_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.he4_factor","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L201-L209","doc":"**⁴He factor: two pn pairs.**\n\n⁴He is Borromean² — two pos-neg pairs — giving `(1 - h²)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pn_pair_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pn_pair_factor","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L193-L199","doc":"**Positive-negative pair factor.**\n\nOne positive and one negative crossing gives `1 - h²` —\nthe fundamental amphichiral unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_factor","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L185-L191","doc":"**Deuteron chirality.**\n\nThe deuteron has one positive pn crossing (single\ninter-nucleon braiding), so `a_D = 1 + h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.amphichiral_factor_k_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.amphichiral_factor_k_pairs","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L175-L183","doc":"Inductive amphichiral factor for `k` positive-then-negative\npairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_append","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L161-L173","doc":"The chirality factor over an append is the product of the\nchirality factors.  (List.foldl distributes over append\nfor an associative operation with the correct start value.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_replicate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_replicate","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L150-L159","doc":"The chirality factor over `List.replicate k c` is the\nper-crossing factor to the `k`-th power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.amphichiral_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.amphichiral_factor","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L136-L148","doc":"**Amphichiral collapse.**\n\nFor an amphichiral braid (equal positive and negative pn\ncrossings, paired consecutively), the chirality factor\nreduces to a power of `1 - h²`:\n\n  a_K(amphichiral, k pos-neg pairs) = (1 - h²)^k.\n\nThis is the derivation of the paper's T, ³He, ⁴He values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tau_sym_pos_deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tau_sym_pos_deviation","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L105-L134","doc":"**Key identity: per-generator symmetric-channel deviation.**\n\nFor a single generator with sign `s`, the symmetric-channel\ndeviation is\n\n  τ_sym([σ^s]) - τ_sym([σ^{-s}]) = s · h\n\nwhere `h = q - q⁻¹`.  This is the core content of the paper's\n\"dual-space\" derivation: the per-crossing chirality factor\n`1 + s·h` is `1` (identity channel) plus `s·h` (symmetric\ndeviation).\n\nThe non-trivial content: the symmetric-channel deviation\nis exactly the Hecke parameter h = q − q⁻¹.\n\nConcretely, the symmetric-channel character of a positive\ncrossing σ⁺ is q (eigenvalue of T = qE + q⁻¹·1 on the\nsym-projection), and the identity-channel value is 1, so the\ndeviation is q − 1.  But the Hecke-relation eigenvalues are\n{q, −q⁻¹} not {q, 1}, so the relevant \"deviation from\nidentity-symmetric mean\" reads off as h = q − q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tauSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tauSym","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L92-L103","doc":"The symmetric-channel trace τ_sym on the Hecke generators.\n\nIn the 1-dimensional symmetric representation V_{(n)} of\nH_n(q), the generator σ_i acts by scalar `q` (and σ_i⁻¹ by\n`q⁻¹`).  The symmetric-channel \"trace\" of σ_i on V_{(n)} is\ntherefore the eigenvalue `q` itself.\n\nFor a product braid word the trace multiplies: τ_sym on a\nword `σ_{i_1}^{ε_1} ⋯ σ_{i_k}^{ε_k}` is\n`q^{ε_1 + ⋯ + ε_k}` — which equals `q^(writhe)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_cons","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L85-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_nil","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L80-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L72-L78","doc":"The total chirality factor of a braid word: product over\nall pn crossings of the per-crossing factors.\n\nImplemented as `List.prod` (associative product) so that\n`_cons` and `_append` lemmas are immediate. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:frobenius-self-pairing-chirality","label":"def:frobenius-self-pairing-chirality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-self-pairing-chirality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingChiralityFactor_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingChiralityFactor_neg","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L67-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingChiralityFactor_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingChiralityFactor_pos","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L62-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossingChiralityFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossingChiralityFactor","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L52-L60","doc":"Per-crossing chirality factor.\n\nAt a positive crossing: `1 + h`.\nAt a negative crossing: `1 - h`.\n\nThis is the content of the symmetric-channel deviation\n`τ_sym(σ) - τ_sym(σ⁻¹) = sign·h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.neg_toReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.neg_toReal","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L49-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.pos_toReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.pos_toReal","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L47-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.toReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.toReal","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L42-L45","doc":"Numeric value of a crossing sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqCrossingSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqCrossingSign","kind":"instance","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.neg","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign.pos","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingSign","kind":"inductive","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-dual-space-derivation.lean#L36-L40","doc":"Sign of a crossing ∈ {+1, -1}. ","signatureChunk":0}]}